# AMRAP agent rules (SvelteKit)

Follow the full project standards in **`AGENTS.md`** (this package root) for every change. `CLAUDE.md` also points there.

## Non-negotiables

- **pnpm only** — never npm/yarn
- **Do not run `pnpm run build`** unless the user asks or the task is build/CI failure
- **Read SvelteKit docs** in `node_modules/@sveltejs/kit/` when unsure about load functions, form actions, hooks, or adapters — do not assume Next.js patterns
- **Reuse / extend shared components** — one Input, Button, FormField pattern, etc.; extract on the second copy; no one-off duplicates
- **i18n** — all user-facing strings in `es` + `en` dictionaries in the same change; no hardcoded UI copy
- **Folder structure** — `src/routes/`, `src/lib/`, `static/`; colocate form actions in `+page.server.ts` / `+server.ts`
- **Product docs** — if business rules or general AMRAP behavior change, update `README.md` in the same change
- **Product flows** — if a feature, screen, nav item, role/permission, or user flow changes, update `docs/product-flows.md` in the same change (**shipped · partial · planned**)
- **Database migrations** — every DB change is a **new** file in **`supabase/migrations/`**; never edit an already-applied migration; update `docs/database.md` in the same change
- **Default app is SvelteKit at repo root** — legacy Next.js is only under `amrap-next/`
- **Verify Supabase project before push** — confirm project name + ref before any remote DB command; ask if ambiguous
- **Validate inputs on the server** with Zod (`src/lib/validation/schemas.ts`); map failures via `zodFieldErrors` + `FormField` `error` (dictionary copy)
- **Backend on the server** — `+page.server.ts` load/actions, `+server.ts` route handlers, `hooks.server.ts`; use `src/lib/supabase/server.ts`; never expose service keys to the client
- **Design system + responsive + a11y** — CSS variables, labels, focus, icon `aria-label`s; follow **Responsive UI / UX** in `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/responsive-ux.mdc`
- **Tenant/RLS/secrets** — session-scoped data; service role server-only
- **E2E (Playwright)** — every new/changed user-facing feature ships with coverage under `e2e/<role>/` (or an explicit PR note why deferred). Keep `docs/product-flows.md` in sync. See `AGENTS.md` → *Testing / E2E* and `e2e/README.md`.
